    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70655" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηλεῖτις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νη-, ἀλείτης, ἀλιταίνω</span>) fem.
			Adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>guiltless, unoffending,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναῖκας . . , αἵ τέ σ᾽ ἀτιμάζουσι
					καὶ αἳ νηλείτιδές εἰσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					16.317
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				19.498
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				22.418
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηλιτέες, νηλητέες</span> are
			vv. ll.; <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i> interpr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμαρτωλοί,
			πολυαμάρτητοι,</span> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νη</span>-
			intens.)</div>
